{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\n     4\t- D726, \"同意\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\",\n     5\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \"it is built with the release work, which is not started\";\n     6\t- D756, \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\".\n     7\t\n     8\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\n     9\t\n    10\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\n    11\tcould reach a reader:\n    12\t- the idea card;\n    13\t- the closing text;\n    14\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\n    15\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\n    16\t- a translated export;\n    17\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\n    18\t\n    19\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\n    20\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\n    21\t\n    22\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\n    23\t\n    24\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\n    25\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\n    26\t- **Its idea input** reads \"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\".\n    27\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\n    28\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \"around $1 trillion\" for 2027 spending;\n    29\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\n    30\t\n    31\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\n    32\t\n    33\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\n    34\t\n    35\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\n    36\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\n    37\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\n    38\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\n    39\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\n    40\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\n    41\t  - no live POC service;\n    42\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\n    43\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\n    44\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\n    45\t\n    46\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\n    47\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n    48\t  - the question and its id;\n    49\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\n    50\t  - the marker \"Forecast unavailable\".\n    51\t\n    52\t  Nothing else is listed:\n    53\t  - no ladder;\n    54\t  - no band, label or condition;\n    55\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\n    56\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n    57\t  - no closing band (\"closed\" only);\n    58\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\n    59\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n    60\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n    61\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\n    62\t  delivered card.\n    63\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\n    64\t  later choice for Alex.\n    65\t\n    66\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\n    67\t\n    68\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\n    69\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\n    70\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\n    71\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\n    72\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\n    73\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\n    74\t\n    75\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\n    76\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\n    77\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\n    78\t\n    79\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\n    80\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\n    81\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\n    82\t\n    83\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\n    84\t\n    85\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\n    86\tbinary event such as \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\n    87\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\n    88\t\n    89\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n    90\t\n    91\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\n    92\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\n    93\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\n    94\t  readers would see.\n    95\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\n    96\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\n    97\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\n    98\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\n    99\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n   100\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\n   101\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\n   102\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\n   103\t  `why_changed`.\n   104\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\n   105\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\n   106\t\n   107\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\n   108\t\n   109\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\n   110\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\n   111\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\n   112\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\n   113\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\n   114\t  - an event question;\n   115\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\n   116\t  - a real closing switch;\n   117\t  - an idea.\n   118\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n   119\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n   120\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n   121\t- **Mutants:**\n   122\t  - an extra field;\n   123\t  - a fetch left on;\n   124\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\n   125\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\n   126\t\n   127\t  Each must fail.\n   128\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\n   129\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n   130\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\n   131\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\n   132\t    prose rule.\n   133\t- **The $0 release check.**\n   134\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n   135\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\n   136\t    final band there.\n   137\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\n   138\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n   139\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n   140\t\n   141\t## 6. Not in scope\n   142\t\n   143\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n   144\t- The closed v13s line.\n   145\t- Other open defects.\n   146\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\n   147\t- The POC's own behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A7 '\"'^##.*D(726|756|757|758)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '125,160p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A7 '\"'^##.*D(726|756|757|758)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '125,160p'\"","aggregated_output":"10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n10992-\n10993-- **The questions** (after D725):\n10994-  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n10995-    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n10996-    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n10997-  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n10998-    (recommended); 暂不定.\n--\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\n11800-\n11801-- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23/`, the\n11802-  verdict sealed in `verdict.json`):\n11803-  - STOP, complete. Joint usable in 3 of 9 pairs against the registered 8; separate 0 of 9.\n11804-  - 5 published defects, all singleton deciding gaps (O 1, E 1, S 3): unsized adjustments decide the band.\n11805-  - Spend $0.3339 of the $0.50 cap.\n11806-  - The checker refused 22 of 36 first attempts (61.1%): 21 carry a luna violation of a stated format rule, and 1 is a\n--\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n11824-\n11825-- **The question** (after D755): \"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\"\n11826-  - Options:\n11827-    - \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\": the council's consensus;\n11828-    - \"换更强的模型再小测一次\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\n11829-    - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n11830-- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n--\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n11843-\n11844-- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \"Forecast\n11845-  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n11846-  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\n11847-- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\n11848-  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\n11849-  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\n--\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n11868-\n11869-- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\n11870-  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n11871-  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\n11872-- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\n11873-  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\n11874-     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\n   125\t  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\n   126\t  same key or rule.\n   127\t- **Code over prose.** A contract that code or a schema can enforce (an enum over allowed keys, a shape) is enforced there, and stays out\n   128\t  of prompts and documents.\n   129\t- **One word per concept.** The glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section Glossary; D36, D163) names each concept once, and\n   130\t  `docs/check.py` fails on a word it rules out. A new concept gets its row and its ruled-out words in the same change; a new ruled-out\n   131\t  word must catch the sentence it was written against and pass the corrected one.\n   132\t- **Identity.** An identifier names one thing for the life of its scope; a changed thing gets a new id. Equal values alone never\n   133\t  establish identity (D248 boundary 7, the same statement carried by several outlets, is a chosen exception, switched on only after its\n   134\t  merge risk on the gold and the accuracy of the original speaker and day fields are measured).\n   135\t- **Explicit inputs.** Library code takes runtime paths and configuration as arguments. A branch a run takes comes from its\n   136\t  configuration, never from whether an environment variable happens to be set; a configured step whose credential is missing refuses\n   137\t  the run. A component that sends a model call uses the transport its caller passes.\n   138\t- **Never order by the wall clock.** It steps both ways; order comes from a sequence the program owns: dispatch's sequence number. The\n   139\t  stream never reads the calendar; only pull mode acts on time, with its \"now\" passed in (D12, D13, D31).\n   140\t- **Strictness is code too.** A check added to prevent defects can itself fail; accept it on real data, not samples.\n   141\t- **Style.** Descriptive names. Docstrings and comments state behaviour, not history. The standard library unless a measured need\n   142\t  justifies a dependency.\n   143\t- **Frontend presentation.** Follow the sentence-case and metadata-separator rules in `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md#presentation-rules`.\n   144\t\n   145\t## 4. Tests\n   146\t\n   147\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\n   148\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\n   149\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\n   150\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\n   151\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\n   152\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\n   153\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\n   154\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\n   155\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\n   156\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\n   157\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\n   158\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\n   159\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\"never called\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\n   160\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | head -270'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | head -270'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"Read-only answers over the views ledger, as of a calendar day (docs/poc/service.md).\n     2\t\n     3\tNothing here reads the clock (D12, D13): every function takes `as_of`, a day, and the default is the ledger's last\n     4\tcompleted day. A row is visible as of a day when the sequence number it was written under belongs to an item or a\n     5\tdaily round dated on or before that day. Nothing here writes.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\timport json\n     8\timport re\n     9\timport sqlite3\n    10\tfrom decimal import Decimal\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom . import vocabulary\n    13\tfrom .views import store\n    14\t\n    15\tTIER_FACT = vocabulary.TIERS[0]          # 'fact'; a legacy ledger's '发生的事' compares equal through vocabulary.canonical\n    16\tCOMPARATORS = ('>=', '<', '=')\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef open_ledger(path):\n    20\t    \"\"\"A read-only connection to a views database.\"\"\"\n    21\t    return store.open_read_only(path)\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\tdef default_as_of(conn):\n    25\t    \"\"\"Today's default day: the last completed day, or a legacy ledger's last judgement day. Read only through `resolve_bound`.\"\"\"\n    26\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) or conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from judgements').fetchone()[0]\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\tclass FirstDayNotCompleted(ValueError):\n    30\t    \"\"\"The store holds processing steps and no completed day: its first day is still in progress, and nothing is served from it\n    31\t    (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 4; open defect 10).\"\"\"\n    32\t\n    33\t    def __init__(self):\n    34\t        super().__init__(\"the store's first day has not completed\")\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\tclass BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\n    38\t    \"\"\"An explicit upper bound later than the store's last completed day: refused, naming that day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\"\"\"\n    39\t\n    40\t    def __init__(self, requested, last_completed_day):\n    41\t        self.requested, self.last_completed_day = requested, last_completed_day\n    42\t        super().__init__(f'day not completed: {requested} is after the last completed day {last_completed_day}')\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tclass RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\n    46\t    \"\"\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\"\"\"\n    47\t\n    48\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\n    49\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\n    50\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    54\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\n    59\t\n    60\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\n    61\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\n    62\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\n    63\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\"\"\"\n    64\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    65\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\n    66\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    67\t    if not bound:\n    68\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\n    69\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\n    70\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\n    71\t    return bound\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\n    75\t    \"\"\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\n    76\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\n    77\t    start is included; a client polling \"what changed since the day I last saw\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\n    78\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\"\"\"\n    79\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\n    80\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\n    81\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\n    82\t    return end\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\n    89\t    \"\"\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\n    90\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\n    91\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\"\"\"\n    92\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\n    93\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\n    94\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\n    95\t        return entry[2]\n    96\t    cache = {}\n    97\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\n    98\t        cache[seq] = day\n    99\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\n   100\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\n   101\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\n   102\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\n   103\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\n   104\t    return cache\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\n   108\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\n   112\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\n   113\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\t# ---------- views\n   117\t\n   118\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   119\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   123\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\n   124\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\n   125\t            return bool(row['open'])\n   126\t    return True\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   130\t    \"\"\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\"\"\"\n   131\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\n   132\t    if not rows:\n   133\t        return None\n   134\t    last = rows[-1]\n   135\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\n   136\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\n   137\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\n   138\t            previous = row['rung']\n   139\t            break\n   140\t        since = row['publication_day']\n   141\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\n   142\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\n   146\t    \"\"\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\n   147\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\n   148\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\"\"\"\n   149\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   150\t    out = []\n   151\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\n   152\t        record = dict(record)\n   153\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   154\t            continue\n   155\t        is_open = is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)\n   156\t        if not include_closed and not is_open:\n   157\t            continue\n   158\t        out.append({'view_id': record['view_id'], 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\n   159\t                    'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'open': is_open,\n   160\t                    'dependencies': [d['view_id'] for d in dependencies(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)], 'dependants': dependants(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)})\n   161\t    return out\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\tdef views(conn, object_id=None, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\n   165\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   166\t    rows = conn.execute('select * from views' + (' where object_id=?' if object_id else '') + ' order by created_seq', (object_id,) if object_id else ()).fetchall()\n   167\t    out = []\n   168\t    for record in rows:\n   169\t        record = dict(record)\n   170\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   171\t            continue\n   172\t        if not include_closed and not is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of):\n   173\t            continue\n   174\t        out.append(view(conn, record['view_id'], as_of, record=record))\n   175\t    return out\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\tdef dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   179\t    \"\"\"The view's dependencies recorded on or before the day, each pointing at the target resolved on or before it.\"\"\"\n   180\t    out = []\n   181\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\n   182\t        if not visible(conn, dep['seq'], as_of):\n   183\t            continue\n   184\t        target = dep['depends_on']\n   185\t        for res in conn.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc', (dep['dependency_id'],)):\n   186\t            if visible(conn, res['seq'], as_of):\n   187\t                target = res['resolved_to']\n   188\t                break\n   189\t        out.append({'view_id': target, 'direction': dep['direction'], 'wait_chain_view_id': dep['wait_chain_view_id'], 'wait_year': dep['wait_year'], 'since_day': day_of_seq(conn, dep['seq'])})\n   190\t    return out\n   191\t\n   192\t\n   193\tdef dependants(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   194\t    \"\"\"The views recorded on or before the day as depending on this one (directly or by a resolution).\"\"\"\n   195\t    direct = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\n   196\t    resolved = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select d.view_id, r.seq from dependency_resolutions r join dependencies d on d.dependency_id=r.dependency_id where r.resolved_to=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\n   197\t    return sorted(set(direct + resolved))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\tdef view(conn, view_id, as_of=None, record=None):\n   201\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   202\t    record = record or store.view(conn, view_id)\n   203\t    if not record or not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   204\t        return None\n   205\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   206\t    state = state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of)\n   207\t    if state:\n   208\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\n   209\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\n   210\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\n   211\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\n   212\t    return {\n   213\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\n   214\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\n   215\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\n   216\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\n   217\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\n   218\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\n   219\t    }\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t# ---------- evidence\n   223\t\n   224\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\n   225\t    \"\"\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\n   226\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\"\"\"\n   227\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\n   228\t    if not piece:\n   229\t        return None\n   230\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\n   231\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\n   232\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\n   233\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\n   234\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\n   235\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\n   239\t    \"\"\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\"\"\"\n   240\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   241\t    out = []\n   242\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\n   243\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\n   244\t            continue\n   245\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n   246\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\n   247\t            continue\n   248\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\n   249\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\n   250\t            continue\n   251\t        out.append(piece)\n   252\t    return out\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\t# ---------- history\n   256\t\n   257\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\n   258\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\n   259\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\n   260\t    judgements = []\n   261\t    previous = None\n   262\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\n   263\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\n   264\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\n   265\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\n   266\t        previous = row['rung']\n   267\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\n   268\t            judgements.append(entry)\n   269\t    arrivals = {}\n   270\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '23,105p;208,275p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '23,105p;208,275p'\"","aggregated_output":"    23\t\n    24\tdef default_as_of(conn):\n    25\t    \"\"\"Today's default day: the last completed day, or a legacy ledger's last judgement day. Read only through `resolve_bound`.\"\"\"\n    26\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) or conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from judgements').fetchone()[0]\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\tclass FirstDayNotCompleted(ValueError):\n    30\t    \"\"\"The store holds processing steps and no completed day: its first day is still in progress, and nothing is served from it\n    31\t    (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 4; open defect 10).\"\"\"\n    32\t\n    33\t    def __init__(self):\n    34\t        super().__init__(\"the store's first day has not completed\")\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\tclass BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\n    38\t    \"\"\"An explicit upper bound later than the store's last completed day: refused, naming that day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\"\"\"\n    39\t\n    40\t    def __init__(self, requested, last_completed_day):\n    41\t        self.requested, self.last_completed_day = requested, last_completed_day\n    42\t        super().__init__(f'day not completed: {requested} is after the last completed day {last_completed_day}')\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tclass RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\n    46\t    \"\"\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\"\"\"\n    47\t\n    48\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\n    49\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\n    50\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    54\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\n    59\t\n    60\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\n    61\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\n    62\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\n    63\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\"\"\"\n    64\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    65\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\n    66\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    67\t    if not bound:\n    68\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\n    69\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\n    70\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\n    71\t    return bound\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\n    75\t    \"\"\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\n    76\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\n    77\t    start is included; a client polling \"what changed since the day I last saw\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\n    78\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\"\"\"\n    79\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\n    80\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\n    81\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\n    82\t    return end\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\n    89\t    \"\"\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\n    90\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\n    91\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\"\"\"\n    92\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\n    93\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\n    94\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\n    95\t        return entry[2]\n    96\t    cache = {}\n    97\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\n    98\t        cache[seq] = day\n    99\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\n   100\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\n   101\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\n   102\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\n   103\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\n   104\t    return cache\n   105\t\n   208\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\n   209\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\n   210\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\n   211\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\n   212\t    return {\n   213\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\n   214\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\n   215\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\n   216\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\n   217\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\n   218\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\n   219\t    }\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t# ---------- evidence\n   223\t\n   224\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\n   225\t    \"\"\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\n   226\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\"\"\"\n   227\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\n   228\t    if not piece:\n   229\t        return None\n   230\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\n   231\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\n   232\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\n   233\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\n   234\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\n   235\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\n   239\t    \"\"\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\"\"\"\n   240\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   241\t    out = []\n   242\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\n   243\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\n   244\t            continue\n   245\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n   246\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\n   247\t            continue\n   248\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\n   249\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\n   250\t            continue\n   251\t        out.append(piece)\n   252\t    return out\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\t# ---------- history\n   256\t\n   257\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\n   258\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\n   259\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\n   260\t    judgements = []\n   261\t    previous = None\n   262\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\n   263\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\n   264\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\n   265\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\n   266\t        previous = row['rung']\n   267\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\n   268\t            judgements.append(entry)\n   269\t    arrivals = {}\n   270\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\n   271\t        day = day_of_seq(conn, link['seq'])\n   272\t        if day and from_day <= day <= to_day:\n   273\t            piece = store.evidence(conn, link['evidence_id'])\n   274\t            bucket = arrivals.setdefault(day, {'evidence': 0, 'facts': 0})\n   275\t            bucket['evidence'] += 1\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
