{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'legacy|default_as_of|boundnotcompleted|firstdaynotcompleted' tests/test_service*.py docs/poc/service.md src/hivemind/bundle.py\"","aggregated_output":"docs/poc/service.md:36:Use structured numeric rung bounds where supplied; the legacy path parses text. Bounds must form an unbroken, non-overlapping partition. Each shared boundary belongs to exactly one band; a lowest money range may begin at zero. A non-money or unparseable ladder returns `evaluable: false` with a reason.\ndocs/poc/service.md:38:Legacy parsing recognises comparator phrases, ranges, postfix bounds and exact amounts. It follows the clauses specifying the amount, ignoring preceding datelines and later remarks. A bare nonzero number is not automatically money; percentages, gigawatts and years are not dollar amounts. Chinese magnitude units remain accepted input. For example, 269.79 hundred-million dollars is exactly $26,979,000,000. The original-language regression strings remain in tests and the historical source document.\ntests/test_service.py:27:def test_default_as_of_is_the_last_completed_day(ledger):\ntests/test_service.py:28:    assert service.default_as_of(ledger) == '2026-08-15'\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:47:    ladder; 'no table' for a store without that table (a legacy ledger); 'no row' when the store has the table and no row for the\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:67:    legacy ledger, for a view with no row, and before the view's creation at as_of; [] when the row lists none. A malformed row,\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:84:    direction (page-contract/DESIGN.md): (None, None) for a legacy ledger; ('unrecorded', None) for a view with no row in a store\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
