{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'Fake only|Mutate on|positive control|entry point' AGENTS.md; rg -n 'def last_completed_day|def first_day_in_progress' src/hivemind/views/store.py; rg -n '\"'^##.*D(726|756|757|758)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"151:- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\n158:- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\n160:- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\n165:- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\n490:def last_completed_day(conn):\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
