{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md | tail -31'","aggregated_output":"    22\t   - fixtures that separate every branch, with a condition-only resolved number, unresolved numbers with and without a key, the\n    23\t     served ledger's \"Restriction adopted\" labels, and a legacy store with no key table;\n    24\t   - a manifest-prose mutant;\n    25\t   - a mutant that writes judgement text into `one_line`;\n    26\t   - writer refusal exercised through the builder;\n    27\t   - the known leaks exported at 2026-08-25 and 2026-08-28.\n    28\t9. **The open points:** no idea submission, its acceptance carried forward; `object` and `kind` dropped; groups out; floor removed.\n    29\t10. **The decisive acceptance case,** as stated in `codex-r74.md`. It also keeps `e3597`'s genuine $390 billion analyst quote as a\n    30\t    control.\n    31\t\n    32\t## Disputed: rewriting evidence summaries that state a calculated figure\n    33\t\n    34\t`codex-r74.md` §1 asks the release to use the source wording where a summary introduces a calculated figure (`e3238`: \"more than\n    35\t$40 billion\" from \"more than double\"). I propose keeping the summary as extraction stored it, for four reasons.\n    36\t\n    37\t- **What D726 withholds is the judge's output:** the band, the forecast text and the history (Alex: \"档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'\").\n    38\t  The evidence is the extraction step's reading of a source, and extraction runs on the frozen production prompt (v74i).\n    39\t- **Extraction never sees the system's forecast.** The request lists each open question only as id, object, due day, question and a\n    40\t  \"takes\" line (`src/hivemind/placement.py:59-61`, `:19-42`; `src/hivemind/extraction.py:398-400`). No rung, label or judged position\n    41\t  is shown. A summary therefore cannot echo our forecast; its figures come from the item.\n    42\t- **The measured rule would mostly remove harmless text.** \"Every number in the summary must be in the quote\" fails on 25.6%, 25.2%\n    43\t  and 25.4% of the evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and on 35.0% in the served ledger\n    44\t  (`scratchpad oneline_census.py`). In a random sample of 24 failures, 23 are context made explicit: a year for \"this year\", a date\n    45\t  for \"Monday\", \"Q3\", \"FY2027\", a product name such as \"H200\", an amount from the previous sentence. One (served `e2798`) restates\n    46\t  \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\". The rule would be a patch on the extraction module, which this\n    47\t  slice has not taken up (AGENTS, \"Authority and scope\").\n    48\t- **\"Amounts as quoted\"** in the design meant the release computes or converts nothing. Revision 2 says so in those words. The\n    49\t  property (a summary can restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source) is disclosed in the design, not built.\n    50\t\n    51\tIf the council still disagrees, AGENTS says to take the cheaper, reversible course. Keeping the stored summary is cheaper and is\n    52\treversible: the field can be dropped from the allow-list in a later version.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
