{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '174,190p;268,312p'\"","aggregated_output":"   174\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\n   175\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\n   176\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n   177\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n   178\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\n   179\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\n   180\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n   181\t| `--out` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\n   182\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   183\t| `OSError` while writing, checking or moving | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   184\t| Crash while staging | this build's uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. It blocks no later build, and the user may delete it | staging only | — |\n   185\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\n   186\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages in its own folder. The first rename wins; the second refuses on the existing folder and removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\n   187\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\n   188\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\n   189\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\n   190\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n   268\t9. **Package:**\n   269\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\n   270\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\n   271\t   - a changed data byte fails;\n   272\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\n   273\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\n   274\t   - an existing `--out` or staging folder is refused.\n   275\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\n   276\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\n   277\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\n   278\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\n   279\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`.\n   280\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\n   281\t12. **Builder refusal, through the builder.**\n   282\t    - Fault injection: the test wraps `release.release_export`, as the builder calls it in-process, so that it returns the real\n   283\t      export with one evidence `one_line` replaced. The closed set still holds.\n   284\t    - Expected: exit non-zero, no `--out`, and the builder's staging folder removed.\n   285\t    - Removing the builder's staged check must make this test fail. This is the one fake in the suite: an injected writer fault, not\n   286\t      an external service.\n   287\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package, then the items database copied with one referenced item deleted:\n   288\t    `check` refuses, and the package is left in place.\n   289\t14. **Two builds aimed at one `--out`.** The second refuses. The winner's package passes `check`, and no staging folder of the winner\n   290\t    is removed by the loser.\n   291\t15. **Files:** a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails, and so does a data file with a repeated `one_line` member name.\n   292\t16. **Bound validation:** `2026-08-99` refused; a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\n   293\t\n   294\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\n   295\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\n   296\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\n   297\t- the event test removed;\n   298\t- the Yes/No test removed;\n   299\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\n   300\t- manifest keys unchecked;\n   301\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\n   302\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\n   303\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\n   304\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\n   305\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\n   306\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\n   307\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package`;\n   308\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\n   309\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\n   310\t- the switch reason emitted;\n   311\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\n   312\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '106,163p'\"","aggregated_output":"   106\t\n   107\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\n   108\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\n   112\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\n   113\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\t# ---------- views\n   117\t\n   118\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   119\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   123\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\n   124\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\n   125\t            return bool(row['open'])\n   126\t    return True\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   130\t    \"\"\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\"\"\"\n   131\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\n   132\t    if not rows:\n   133\t        return None\n   134\t    last = rows[-1]\n   135\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\n   136\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\n   137\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\n   138\t            previous = row['rung']\n   139\t            break\n   140\t        since = row['publication_day']\n   141\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\n   142\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\n   146\t    \"\"\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\n   147\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\n   148\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\"\"\"\n   149\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   150\t    out = []\n   151\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\n   152\t        record = dict(record)\n   153\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   154\t            continue\n   155\t        is_open = is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)\n   156\t        if not include_closed and not is_open:\n   157\t            continue\n   158\t        out.append({'view_id': record['view_id'], 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\n   159\t                    'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'open': is_open,\n   160\t                    'dependencies': [d['view_id'] for d in dependencies(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)], 'dependants': dependants(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)})\n   161\t    return out\n   162\t\n   163\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
